      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KALIMERA (3) hit the ground running from the squeeze draw with a slick early split, holding on for a minor placing when third and beaten 1.5 lengths at Wentworth Park over 520m in 30.06. Good beginner aided by a nice draw. Well placed and gets his chance. COBY KADE (7) was strongly fancied latest and proved too good with a 2.5 lengths win at Richmond in a handy 22.80. Wide box to overcome but likes the trip. Safe beginner but wide box to overcome and will need some luck. Can continue on with her winning form. RUGGED ETHICS (4) produced a modest effort most recently when seventh at Wentworth Park over 520m behind Back Tomorrow (30.65) in a Grade 5. Expected to feature in the finish. LADY LLORONA (2) placed last time out so worth considering.",
